Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.3 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer. The obligations of Acquirer to consummate the Closing are subject to the satisfaction (or waiver by Acquirer) prior to the Closing of the following conditions: (a) Representations and Warranties. (i) The representations and warranties set forth in Article V (other than those in Sections 5.1, 5.2(b), and 5.7) shall be true and correct in all respects (disregarding all materiality and \u201cMaterial Adverse Effect\u201d qualifiers) as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date as if made anew as of the Closing Date, except where the failure of such representations and warranties to be true and correct would not reasonably be expected to have a Material Adverse Effect. The representations and warranties in Sections 5.1, 5.2(b), and 5.7 shall be true and correct in all material respects as of the date hereof and as of the Closing Date as if made anew as of the Closing Date. (Page 92)
